{
	title: 'Web clients resync after dropped events',
	spec: 'Invariant restored: a web client never silently misses host events; it notices and resyncs. The host serves /ws with closeOnBackpressureLimit: Bun drops a send past its 16 MB backpressure limit, so the host closes that socket and the client reconnects, reopening its sessions from fresh snapshots and resending pending commands. The first dropped send on a socket writes one diag.log line ("dropped events") naming the client and buffered bytes. Every event host.adapt writes carries seq 1, 2, ... per connection; ws-link strips it before delivery, and on a skipped number closes with 4002 (reason: expected and received seq) and reconnects. The host logs a 4002 close to diag.log ("missed events"). A host message the client cannot parse reaches the user as a warning with the parse error and the start of the raw message, never a silent drop. A timebomb test in src/host/diag.test.ts (normal suite) fails on 2026-12-01 and says how to review: no "missed events" lines means delete the seq; rare "dropped events" means delete that logging; frequent ones mean find why clients fall behind. The backpressure close stays either way.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Cause (22-lid, 2026-10-28): an iPhone page woke from the background; for about 25 s it showed a running session as idle and missed a whole turn, plus the ack of its pending prompt, so the stale pending copy stayed below newer messages. The socket never closed, so nothing resynced. Bun 1.4.4 ws.send returns 0 and discards the message past backpressureLimit (default 16 MB) while the socket stays open; with closeOnBackpressureLimit the sends after the limit return -1 then 0 and Bun closes with 1006. A one-off test (paused raw TCP client, 40 MB of deliveries) logged one line and closed the socket; it was not kept.',
		'The seq is the general detector the user asked for: the cause of the 22-lid gap was not proven, and the backpressure close covers only one cause. A Bun drop closes the socket before the client can see a gap, so "missed events" lines count only losses from other causes. Replay from the seq was rejected: it needs per-connection host buffers, largest exactly when the client is slow. web-update is written before host.adapt and carries no seq; ws-link checks only events that have one.',
		'User likes timebomb tests for temporary instrumentation. A review date in task notes was missed before (s37 composer-debug review 2026-10-15 still open on 2026-10-28). Put a timebomb in the normal suite; web tests run only under ./test-expensive.'
